./test/should-error/assert_real.pf:5.1-5.44: assert can only compare data built from constructors, such as Booleans, numbers, and lists, but
	real(+1) + real(+1)
could not be evaluated: it uses something with no definition (such as a `postulate fun`, or an opaque function of a postulated type such as Real), or an operation that does not apply (such as an out-of-bounds index).
To reason about it, prove a theorem instead.
